<title>USA: U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS FELL IN LATEST WEEK.</title>
<headline>U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS FELL IN LATEST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department report of initial state jobless benefit claims, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Week Ended Initial Claims  4-Week Avg.  Continued Claims</p>
<p>  - 07/12/97     349,000	348,750	Unavailable</p>
<p>  - 07/05/97     377,000	348,500	2,378,000</p>
<p>  - 06/28/97     337,000	339,000	2,388,000-R</p>
<p>  - 06/21/97     332,000	339,250	2,319,000</p>
<p>R-Revised, June 28 Continued Claims from 2,478,000.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast initial jobless claims</p>
</text>
